================================================================================
Third-party code
================================================================================

LOFOP contains no third-party source code.

Every component in this repository -- the LOFOP-Detect model family
(RidgeNet, SwiftNet, DeltaFusion, ApexHead, StencilHead, VertexHead,
SlateHead), the native C++ and CUDA kernels, the assignment solver, the
tracking subsystem (motion model, association, tracker), the data subsystem,
the training engine, and the deployment path -- is an original implementation
written for this project.

Where LOFOP implements a published algorithm or a standard mathematical
method, it does so from the mathematics or the published description, not by
adapting another project's source. Such methods are not themselves
copyrightable; the implementations here are LOFOP's own expression of them.
This applies in particular to:

  * the recursive linear estimator ("Kalman filter") in lofop/tracking/motion.py,
    implemented from the standard predict/correct equations with LOFOP's own
    state parameterisation, naming, and noise model;
  * the assignment problem solver in lofop/ops/assignment.py, implemented from
    the shortest-augmenting-path formulation;
  * standard convolutional patterns (depthwise separable convolution,
    inverted residual blocks, squeeze-and-excitation gating, feature pyramid
    fusion, focal loss, GIoU), which are published techniques implemented
    here directly.

